<tr><td colspan=4><font size=2 face=verdana color=#ffffff>Where shall I begin? To begin its best,they say,to start at the beginning,yet it is also an ending, for there are no beginnings without endings, nor endings without beginnings. It was a dark and stormy night,not unlike many others,a mighty paladin was pacing in front of a cottage,while inside his wife,a powerful wizard in her own,was bearing thier child,or attempting so,for it was not an easy birth,the labor had been long and hard,but at last the moment had arrived. The midwife prepared her tools and with a sorrowful look at the mother,prepared to do her best for both the mother and the child in the battle for life ahead. Minutes later, there was a scream from inside the cottage,the paladin,unable to hold back any longer,flung open the door and gazed upon his wife and the midwife with his newborn son in her hands. With a cry of joy he rushed to his wife's side, but the cry of joy turned into a heartwrenching cry of agony as he lifted his wife's lifeless hand.With a cry like the sound of a breaking heart,the paladin fled out into the storm and was never seen again. Now this might sound like an ending, but as I said before,endings are just the start of beginnings.

The midwife, having no choice,had taken the child to his fathers guild,to be fostered and raised there.The boy,even at an early age was unusually handsome and intelligent, you would assume such would be a boon, but instead was often a curse. For his peers were jelouse of the attention he got, and as children so often can be, were often cruel at times.His one wish had been from earliest memory to become a mighty paladin like his fatherand go to search for his father, but alas he had not inherited his fathers prowess. He did soon find that with his good looks and quick wit he could easily make friends and twas often said that he could charm the beard off a veteran dwarf warrior and the dwarf would even be smiling afterwards. So tis only natural that when he showed unusual apptitude for small cantrips, that the enchanters guild would recruit him and offer him a place among them of his own. He trained hard and excelled at all he attempted,and when he at last had surpassed his novice status,was ready to embark on an adventure he had been seeking to go on since his earliest memory, to seek out his father,whereever he had gone.His feelings over the years had melded until he knew not if it was anger or love he would confront his father with  upon finding him, but search he would, search he must.

Many creatures did he fight on his jorneys, and a few friends did he make, until he met a woodelf druid,and a human warrior in a far desert land. Long did they fight together against the mighty giant spiders,scarabs,and undead of that desert land,and a friendship did bloom in the sands that day,such a friendship that he was invited to something he had never been invited to before,a family,the Norrath Militia family,for at this moment he found that it was not his father Sureall Dreammaster had been seeking, but unknowingly, twas a family to belong to after all. thus is the ending of my story...but as with all endings, it is but the beginning. &nbsp;</font></td></tr>

